1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:04,120
Now everybody lift your hands up!

2
00:00:04,260 --> 00:00:06,201
Sing about what you are dreaming!

3
00:00:06,420 --> 00:00:07,760
Always stand up!

4
00:00:07,960 --> 00:00:09,937
Raise up the flag that can't be beaten!

5
00:00:10,020 --> 00:00:11,440
Gotta keep up!

6
00:00:11,620 --> 00:00:15,697
We'll get past every wall that's
in our wake, go without hesitation!

7
00:00:15,780 --> 00:00:16,840
Hands up!

8
00:00:22,900 --> 00:00:26,617
We just have to press on a little more.

9
00:00:26,700 --> 00:00:30,197
To get to the answers we're looking for.

10
00:00:30,280 --> 00:00:33,297
We came to this new world believing.

11
00:00:33,380 --> 00:00:37,797
That surely someday we
just might find the way.

12
00:00:37,880 --> 00:00:42,897
All the pieces of our dreams
have now come together.

13
00:00:42,980 --> 00:00:45,357
Our bonds won't waver.

14
00:00:45,440 --> 00:00:47,837
With our dreaming hand.

15
00:00:47,920 --> 00:00:49,880
Let's head on towards.

16
00:00:50,660 --> 00:00:52,697
A bright new future.

17
00:00:52,780 --> 00:00:56,537
Now everybody lift your hands up.

18
00:00:56,620 --> 00:00:58,597
Sing about what you are dreaming.

19
00:00:58,680 --> 00:01:00,217
Always stand up.

20
00:01:00,300 --> 00:01:02,397
Raise up the flag that you believe in.

21
00:01:02,480 --> 00:01:03,957
Gotta keep up.

22
00:01:04,040 --> 00:01:06,317
We'll get past everyone that's in our way.

23
00:01:06,400 --> 00:01:08,400
Let's head on never stopping.

24
00:01:09,680 --> 00:01:11,337
Only look up.

25
00:01:11,420 --> 00:01:13,337
Keep your head up way up high.

26
00:01:13,420 --> 00:01:15,037
Always step up.

27
00:01:15,120 --> 00:01:17,017
If waves are rough, jump to the sky.

28
00:01:17,100 --> 00:01:18,797
Never give up.

29
00:01:18,880 --> 00:01:20,757
Our wishes, they will come together.

30
00:01:20,840 --> 00:01:23,200
And lead us on for the future.

31
00:01:24,640 --> 00:01:27,837
We drift on riding the waves.

32
00:01:27,920 --> 00:01:30,717
Towards another shore day by day.

33
00:01:30,800 --> 00:01:35,497
There are many meetings, many goodbyes.

34
00:01:35,580 --> 00:01:37,840
Underneath the flag we fly.

35
00:01:41,060 --> 00:01:43,697
I'll remember the pain within.

36
00:01:43,780 --> 00:01:45,877
I'll keep it in my heart forever.

37
00:01:45,960 --> 00:01:47,977
And never take it lightly.

38
00:01:48,060 --> 00:01:49,837
But I won't surrender.

39
00:01:49,920 --> 00:01:52,037
This freedom I will keep in mind.

40
00:01:52,120 --> 00:01:54,637
I'll keep holding on, never stop it.

41
00:01:54,720 --> 00:01:57,437
Now everybody lift your hands up.

42
00:01:57,520 --> 00:01:59,517
Sing about what you are dreaming.

43
00:01:59,600 --> 00:02:01,177
Always stand up.

44
00:02:01,260 --> 00:02:03,337
Raise up the flag that you believe in.

45
00:02:03,420 --> 00:02:04,897
Gotta keep up.

46
00:02:04,980 --> 00:02:07,237
We'll get past everyone that's in our way.

47
00:02:07,320 --> 00:02:09,680
Let's head on, never stop it.

48
00:02:10,920 --> 00:02:14,317
Only look up, keep your
head up way up high.

49
00:02:14,400 --> 00:02:17,957
Always step up, if brains
are rough, jump to the sky.

50
00:02:18,040 --> 00:02:21,637
Never give up, our wishes,
they will come together.

51
00:02:21,720 --> 00:02:24,140
And lead us on for the future.

52
00:02:25,040 --> 00:02:26,120
Hands up.

53
00:02:29,940 --> 00:02:32,760
All right, G5, let's step on it!

54
00:02:33,020 --> 00:02:35,257
Captain Tashigi needs us
to save those children!

55
00:02:35,340 --> 00:02:38,240
I guess Caesar's not the
only Logia type here.

56
00:02:38,380 --> 00:02:40,957
I don't know about that, but either
way, she's out of our league.

57
00:02:41,040 --> 00:02:43,057
Hey, Blackleg, while we're on the subject,

58
00:02:43,140 --> 00:02:45,117
why didn't you help when you
started trying to kill us?

59
00:02:45,200 --> 00:02:47,017
You're stronger than
all of us put together.

60
00:02:47,100 --> 00:02:47,930
Get over it.

61
00:02:48,020 --> 00:02:51,340
I won't kick a woman no
matter how evil she is. Huh?

62
00:02:51,680 --> 00:02:52,797
Are you kidding me?

63
00:02:52,880 --> 00:02:55,317
But what if it came down to
a matter of life and death?

64
00:02:55,400 --> 00:02:57,200
I choose death. What?

65
00:02:57,880 --> 00:02:58,710
No way.

66
00:02:59,600 --> 00:03:03,177
They're all in the same crew, but
they're so different from each other.

67
00:03:03,260 --> 00:03:05,077
Yeah, just look at that
pirate hunter's orb.

68
00:03:05,160 --> 00:03:07,157
He seemed like the type
of person who would

69
00:03:07,240 --> 00:03:09,037
chop you to bits if you
even looked at him funny.

70
00:03:09,120 --> 00:03:11,217
Well, he's got a sensitive side, too.

71
00:03:11,300 --> 00:03:12,977
Don't worry about him, though.

72
00:03:13,060 --> 00:03:14,420
He'll find a way out.

73
00:03:14,600 --> 00:03:16,718
And the same thing goes for Tashigi.

74
00:03:17,180 --> 00:03:21,480
All that matters now is tracking
down that group of rugrats so Nami,

75
00:03:21,600 --> 00:03:25,220
Robin, and Tashigi will tell
us we did a good job! Yeah!

76
00:03:26,700 --> 00:03:28,020
Go with your soldiers.

77
00:03:28,580 --> 00:03:29,940
I'll do as I please.

78
00:03:30,260 --> 00:03:31,977
I said I don't need your help.

79
00:03:32,060 --> 00:03:33,997
They're entitled to your opinion.

80
00:03:34,080 --> 00:03:35,020
Oh, really?

81
00:03:37,260 --> 00:03:42,580
If that's how you feel, then am I entitled
to cut you up first, Miss Navy Captain?

82
00:03:42,840 --> 00:03:43,860
I am a pirate.

83
00:03:45,500 --> 00:03:47,520
No, you can't. Huh?

84
00:03:48,320 --> 00:03:50,380
You won't put a scratch on me.

85
00:03:52,360 --> 00:03:54,080
Or her, for that matter.

86
00:03:54,660 --> 00:03:56,100
You think so, huh?

87
00:03:56,320 --> 00:03:57,673
Well, what do you know?

88
00:03:58,960 --> 00:04:01,060
I was just thinking the same thing.

89
00:04:01,820 --> 00:04:02,800
Am I wrong?

90
00:04:04,320 --> 00:04:05,660
you're letting me live

91
00:04:08,480 --> 00:04:10,000
it's because i'm a girl

92
00:04:10,700 --> 00:04:13,229
jeez woman do you ever
shut your damn mouth

93
00:04:14,640 --> 00:04:17,997
listen you get the same exact
face as some chick i knew who

94
00:04:18,080 --> 00:04:21,317
died so i can't stand the sight
of you on top of that i don't

95
00:04:21,400 --> 00:04:23,677
know a thing about you yet and
you're already talking just

96
00:04:23,760 --> 00:04:28,320
like her why the hell are you
copying her just try to be herself

97
00:04:28,840 --> 00:04:31,193
maybe you ought to think before you talk

98
00:04:38,020 --> 00:04:40,397
you think that women aren't as strong you

99
00:04:40,480 --> 00:04:43,017
hold back in a fight so
you can't kill her can

100
00:04:43,100 --> 00:04:46,017
you you're never gonna
succeed that way that's

101
00:04:46,100 --> 00:04:48,806
why i stayed because
you're not up to the task

102
00:04:49,600 --> 00:04:55,060
with the powers that she's got if she
gets near my men i know it won't be pretty

103
00:04:56,800 --> 00:04:59,800
are you trying to say
you're better than me yes

104
00:05:03,360 --> 00:05:04,440
I've had it then

105
00:05:06,280 --> 00:05:09,580
I'm supposed to keep her
claws off my comrades too,

106
00:05:09,720 --> 00:05:13,602
you know As long as someone keeps
her busy, what's the difference?

107
00:05:14,100 --> 00:05:15,657
You shouldn't be so flippant.

108
00:05:15,740 --> 00:05:17,977
Look, we don't have much time.

109
00:05:18,060 --> 00:05:20,236
You'd better run while you still can.

110
00:05:20,660 --> 00:05:21,697
Stay focused.

111
00:05:21,780 --> 00:05:24,017
One bite and you're dead meat.

112
00:05:24,100 --> 00:05:24,957
He's right.

113
00:05:25,040 --> 00:05:28,257
And thanks to you, I've just
discovered his weakness.

114
00:05:28,340 --> 00:05:33,400
You may have your Haki, but that
won't be enough to save you from me!

115
00:05:39,340 --> 00:05:40,280
Cute trick!

116
00:05:40,700 --> 00:05:44,876
You can use Haki to force a power
user like me back to my normal state.

117
00:05:46,220 --> 00:05:49,632
That said, you have to be fast
enough to catch up with me!

118
00:05:51,480 --> 00:05:52,420
Sorry, dear.

119
00:05:55,840 --> 00:05:57,377
You're colder than I thought.

120
00:05:57,460 --> 00:05:58,640
Oh, I'm cold?

121
00:05:58,840 --> 00:06:00,134
You're the snow woman.

122
00:06:00,340 --> 00:06:01,760
Don't you ignore me!

123
00:06:04,460 --> 00:06:06,240
Care for a snowball fight?

124
00:06:06,660 --> 00:06:07,840
Snow rabbit!

125
00:06:12,880 --> 00:06:15,220
Perhaps I underestimated you.

126
00:06:15,580 --> 00:06:17,521
You are Smoker's right-hand girl.

127
00:06:21,220 --> 00:06:22,320
Oh, great!

128
00:06:22,740 --> 00:06:23,880
Once I end you,

129
00:06:24,120 --> 00:06:29,360
I'll go find your troops and say, your
poor captain just couldn't cut it.

130
00:06:46,520 --> 00:06:47,920
It's my shoulder!

131
00:06:48,260 --> 00:06:49,440
She bit it off!

132
00:06:55,000 --> 00:06:56,400
Let go of me!

133
00:06:56,860 --> 00:06:57,720
Damn you!

134
00:06:58,500 --> 00:07:01,080
If I let go, I'll lose my shoulder.

135
00:07:01,540 --> 00:07:05,080
I gave you a chance, but if
you'd rather, I tear you apart.

136
00:07:15,340 --> 00:07:19,357
If you hadn't been running your
mouth, you'd be done with her by now.

137
00:07:19,440 --> 00:07:20,860
But your time's up.

138
00:07:22,180 --> 00:07:24,900
I'm busy, so let's make
this quick, all right?

139
00:07:25,180 --> 00:07:29,533
I could have sworn he wouldn't cut a
woman, but it looks like I was wrong.

140
00:07:29,800 --> 00:07:32,447
He swung at me without
a moment's hesitation.

141
00:07:34,420 --> 00:07:36,000
So you've misjudged me.

142
00:07:36,320 --> 00:07:37,280
How about that?

143
00:07:40,440 --> 00:07:42,240
That was a fatal mistake.

144
00:07:44,380 --> 00:07:47,740
Maybe I don't go around
cutting just anyone, but still.

145
00:07:48,820 --> 00:07:49,650
Well, think.

146
00:07:51,780 --> 00:07:56,060
When you're face to face with an
animal that can rip you to shreds,

147
00:07:56,180 --> 00:07:58,217
you don't take any chances, do you?

148
00:07:58,300 --> 00:08:00,065
You get the hell out of there.

149
00:08:01,840 --> 00:08:03,980
Oh, well. Too late.

150
00:08:06,060 --> 00:08:07,460
What's happening to me?

151
00:08:07,920 --> 00:08:09,640
I can't move my feet.

152
00:08:11,400 --> 00:08:12,840
One sword style.

153
00:08:13,840 --> 00:08:14,920
He'll kill me.

154
00:08:21,560 --> 00:08:23,340
Great dragon shock.

155
00:08:30,820 --> 00:08:33,620
All right, we're done here. It's over.

156
00:08:34,040 --> 00:08:35,100
He got her.

157
00:08:43,560 --> 00:08:44,390
How...

158
00:08:44,473 --> 00:08:46,080
how dare you!

159
00:08:48,260 --> 00:08:49,820
Did she not die?

160
00:08:54,820 --> 00:08:55,760
That's odd.

161
00:08:56,180 --> 00:08:57,960
He didn't use his haki.

162
00:09:10,700 --> 00:09:12,857
She lost control of her body.

163
00:09:12,940 --> 00:09:15,737
She must have been
petrified when she realized

164
00:09:15,820 --> 00:09:18,114
that she'd die if Zoro used his Haki.

165
00:09:20,800 --> 00:09:22,859
I've never seen anything like that.

166
00:09:23,940 --> 00:09:26,077
I wonder what the Straw Hat Pirates were

167
00:09:26,160 --> 00:09:28,925
doing during those two
years they went missing.

168
00:09:29,920 --> 00:09:31,940
How much stronger are they now?

169
00:09:32,560 --> 00:09:33,560
It's amazing.

170
00:09:34,740 --> 00:09:36,600
You're not getting away now!

171
00:09:37,740 --> 00:09:38,800
Autumn rain!

172
00:09:43,560 --> 00:09:44,390
Sorry, bud.

173
00:09:44,473 --> 00:09:45,303
You're finished.

174
00:09:59,120 --> 00:10:00,580
What was all that about?

175
00:10:00,840 --> 00:10:04,417
After everything you said, you
still didn't try to kill that girl.

176
00:10:04,500 --> 00:10:05,330
See?

177
00:10:05,413 --> 00:10:06,420
I was right about you.

178
00:10:06,580 --> 00:10:07,897
And you can't deny it.

179
00:10:07,980 --> 00:10:10,897
I don't recall asking you to
finish my fight for me, Captain.

180
00:10:10,980 --> 00:10:13,300
If you hadn't killed her, I would have.

181
00:10:13,460 --> 00:10:14,680
You just stepped in.

182
00:10:15,040 --> 00:10:16,460
Hey, that's not fair.

183
00:10:16,680 --> 00:10:17,798
You can't say that.

184
00:10:17,920 --> 00:10:19,737
I stepped in because you were leaving.

185
00:10:19,820 --> 00:10:21,120
Nobody forced you.

186
00:10:22,560 --> 00:10:23,420
But hey.

187
00:10:25,380 --> 00:10:27,320
Good job, Miss Four Eyes.

188
00:10:27,640 --> 00:10:30,581
She's dead, so she can't
hurt anyone else anymore.

189
00:10:31,560 --> 00:10:33,678
I don't mind if you take the credit.

190
00:10:34,440 --> 00:10:36,500
Could you be more patronizing?

191
00:10:36,700 --> 00:10:38,582
You think you're better than me?

192
00:10:38,840 --> 00:10:39,740
Pretty much.

193
00:10:49,220 --> 00:10:50,600
We have to go!

194
00:10:50,820 --> 00:10:51,660
Yeah, come on.

195
00:10:54,900 --> 00:10:56,677
Hey, what are you doing, raccoon?

196
00:10:56,760 --> 00:10:57,590
Get off of me!

197
00:10:57,673 --> 00:10:58,503
It's a sedative.

198
00:10:58,586 --> 00:10:59,698
This will help you.

199
00:11:03,340 --> 00:11:06,600
Hey, what happened to me? Candy!

200
00:11:07,240 --> 00:11:09,717
Quick, go after the children! Right.

201
00:11:09,800 --> 00:11:12,060
Get back here with our kitty, Mocha!

202
00:11:13,580 --> 00:11:14,560
Come back!

203
00:11:15,500 --> 00:11:16,540
Milky Hall!

204
00:11:18,340 --> 00:11:19,380
This again?

205
00:11:19,700 --> 00:11:21,597
We won't be able to keep this up long.

206
00:11:21,680 --> 00:11:23,974
How much further does Mocha have to go?

207
00:11:28,460 --> 00:11:29,640
Where to now?

208
00:11:29,900 --> 00:11:31,300
This place is huge!

209
00:11:31,620 --> 00:11:33,796
I don't know which way to go anymore!

210
00:11:43,260 --> 00:11:46,025
The toxic gas is flowing
into the biscuit room.

211
00:11:47,340 --> 00:11:48,377
What's the problem?

212
00:11:48,460 --> 00:11:50,217
The exit's in the other direction.

213
00:11:50,300 --> 00:11:51,130
What?

214
00:11:51,213 --> 00:11:52,117
You could have told me sooner.

215
00:11:52,200 --> 00:11:54,817
Will you at least put me down
before we catch up with my men?

216
00:11:54,900 --> 00:11:56,417
Swallow your pride for once.

217
00:11:56,500 --> 00:11:59,157
It's not like it'll do you
any good if you're dead.

218
00:11:59,240 --> 00:12:00,280
Jeez, what now?

219
00:12:00,540 --> 00:12:01,477
I don't believe it.

220
00:12:01,560 --> 00:12:03,397
Is that the legendary sword shoestring?

221
00:12:03,480 --> 00:12:08,127
Give your hands to yourself and stop
running your mouth, you stupid sword geek.

222
00:12:09,980 --> 00:12:10,810
No!

223
00:12:12,060 --> 00:12:12,890
Mocha?

224
00:12:13,240 --> 00:12:14,070
Ew!

225
00:12:14,153 --> 00:12:16,440
Please stop this! Mocha! Oh, no!

226
00:12:16,700 --> 00:12:18,317
Some of them took another route!

227
00:12:18,400 --> 00:12:20,540
Please! Mocha! Mocha! Mocha!

228
00:12:20,920 --> 00:12:23,857
If they get the candy, we'll
have to start all over again!

229
00:12:23,940 --> 00:12:25,957
We have to get Mocha away from them!

230
00:12:26,040 --> 00:12:29,864
I just want to get away from this
stupid island and go back home!

231
00:12:35,040 --> 00:12:36,057
She ate all of it!

232
00:12:36,140 --> 00:12:38,077
That's not fair! Mocha!

233
00:12:38,160 --> 00:12:39,480
What was she thinking?

234
00:12:39,780 --> 00:12:41,280
No, Gabby!

235
00:12:41,500 --> 00:12:43,660
Can't just look at all! Gabby!

236
00:12:44,420 --> 00:12:45,250
No, ma!

237
00:12:48,000 --> 00:12:48,830
Mocha!

238
00:12:53,900 --> 00:12:56,460
You need to spit them all out right now!

239
00:12:56,660 --> 00:12:58,620
Do you hear me? Mocha!

240
00:13:01,980 --> 00:13:04,840
I told you what those candies really are!

241
00:13:06,000 --> 00:13:07,620
I'm sorry, Chopper.

242
00:13:09,020 --> 00:13:10,640
I had to do it!

243
00:13:12,960 --> 00:13:14,240
They're my friends!

244
00:13:16,920 --> 00:13:18,140
It's not too late!

245
00:13:18,260 --> 00:13:19,907
You can still spit them out!

246
00:13:20,280 --> 00:13:21,220
I promise!

247
00:13:29,640 --> 00:13:32,640
You know what I think we
should do when we grow up?

248
00:13:33,340 --> 00:13:36,880
We should find a ship and
set out for the open sea!

249
00:13:37,560 --> 00:13:38,390
The sea?

250
00:13:39,320 --> 00:13:40,660
Why, to catch fish?

251
00:13:40,880 --> 00:13:43,120
No, dummy, to go on an adventure.

252
00:13:43,600 --> 00:13:46,757
You know, look for islands made
of gold and stuff like that.

253
00:13:46,840 --> 00:13:48,140
That sounds like fun.

254
00:13:48,820 --> 00:13:51,817
When we get better and go home,
we'll be separated, right?

255
00:13:51,900 --> 00:13:53,782
We won't see each other anymore.

256
00:13:54,420 --> 00:13:57,185
That's why we need a
ship, to pick everyone up.

257
00:13:57,720 --> 00:13:59,720
Yeah, cool, let's go.

258
00:14:00,020 --> 00:14:02,491
A bunch of friends having a big adventure.

259
00:14:05,520 --> 00:14:06,937
So, what's the plan?

260
00:14:07,020 --> 00:14:08,037
When do we go?

261
00:14:08,120 --> 00:14:11,277
Let's see.

262
00:14:11,360 --> 00:14:15,817
I don't know when we're 20 years old.

263
00:14:15,900 --> 00:14:20,617
That's like forever from now—waiting for
so long will just make it more exciting!

264
00:14:20,700 --> 00:14:21,530
Yeah,

265
00:14:22,780 --> 00:14:24,997
okay, let's make it a promise.

266
00:14:25,080 --> 00:14:25,910
So

267
00:14:30,640 --> 00:14:33,197
the master is a bad person, yes?

268
00:14:33,280 --> 00:14:35,117
A very bad person!

269
00:14:35,200 --> 00:14:39,020
person But he's always been
so nice to us the candy.

270
00:14:39,220 --> 00:14:42,220
He gives us is yummy and
we get to eat it every day

271
00:14:42,860 --> 00:14:45,920
That's how he trapped you What? But why?

272
00:14:48,160 --> 00:14:50,077
You children aren't...

273
00:14:50,160 --> 00:14:52,337
his test subjects. How...

274
00:14:52,420 --> 00:14:54,640
how do you know? Hey, Mocha!

275
00:14:54,980 --> 00:14:55,860
Open up!

276
00:14:56,020 --> 00:14:58,608
We need to go to the
biscuit room right now!

277
00:14:59,080 --> 00:14:59,910
